   "source": [
    "## 1. Probability distributions\n",
    "\n",
    "### Discrete distributions\n",
    "\n",
    "These distributions describe countable outcomes. Each distribution below has its own short example and visualization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "efc27a85",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%pip -q install numpy scipy matplotlib scikit-learn"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3ca0e4cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import scipy.stats as stats\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score,\n",
    "    mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, r2_score, log_loss\n",
    ")\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(42)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "295f45a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 1. Geometric — (p)\n",
    "\n",
    "Models the number of trials until the first success. Useful for modeling event counts and waiting processes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4f71cfb2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "p, k = 0.35, 3\n",
    "probability = (1-p)**(k-1)*p\n",
    "print(f\"P(first success on trial {k}) = {probability:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "133d9f13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "66af2110",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.geom(p=0.35)\n",
    "x = np.arange(1, 13)\n",
    "plt.bar(x, d.pmf(x)); plt.title('Geometric distribution (p=0.35)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Trials until first success'); plt.ylabel('Probability'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7a98fa27",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 2. Negative Binomial — (r, p)\n",
    "\n",
    "Models the number of failures before a fixed number of successes. Can describe over-dispersed count data used in predictive modeling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "31b139d2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "r, p, failures = 4, 0.45, 3\n",
    "probability = math.comb(failures+r-1, r-1)*p**r*(1-p)**failures\n",
    "print(f\"P({failures} failures before {r} successes) = {probability:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c148daea",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "40e28dc3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.nbinom(n=4, p=0.45)\n",
    "x = np.arange(0, 20)\n",
    "plt.bar(x, d.pmf(x)); plt.title('Negative Binomial (r=4, p=0.45)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Failures'); plt.ylabel('Probability'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2108b6b8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 3. Hypergeometric — (N, K, n)\n",
    "\n",
    "Models sampling without replacement. Useful when observations are drawn from a finite population."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3dc415c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "N, K, n, successes = 40, 12, 8, 3\n",
    "probability = math.comb(K,successes)*math.comb(N-K,n-successes)/math.comb(N,n)\n",
    "print(f\"P({successes} successes in sample) = {probability:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "49d51b9a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a00a4f94",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.hypergeom(M=40, n=12, N=8)\n",
    "x = np.arange(0, 9)\n",
    "plt.bar(x, d.pmf(x)); plt.title('Hypergeometric (N=40, K=12, n=8)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Successes in sample'); plt.ylabel('Probability'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c6c68bae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 4. Poisson — (λ)\n",
    "\n",
    "Models event counts over a fixed interval. Often used for count prediction, arrivals, and incident-rate modeling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "878fedc0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "lam, k = 4, 3\n",
    "probability = math.exp(-lam)*lam**k/math.factorial(k)\n",
    "print(f\"P({k} events) = {probability:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "443b724d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ce078b36",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.poisson(mu=4)\n",
    "x = np.arange(0, 15)\n",
    "plt.bar(x, d.pmf(x)); plt.title('Poisson (λ=4)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Event count'); plt.ylabel('Probability'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b3c3bfa9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 5. Binomial — (n, p)\n",
    "\n",
    "Models the number of successes across a fixed number of independent trials. Useful for binary-outcome and reliability modeling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3859ebf3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "n, p, k = 12, 0.35, 4\n",
    "probability = math.comb(n,k)*p**k*(1-p)**(n-k)\n",
    "print(f\"P({k} successes) = {probability:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "71ed7311",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "672a84e3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.binom(n=12, p=0.35)\n",
    "x = np.arange(0, 13)\n",
    "plt.bar(x, d.pmf(x)); plt.title('Binomial (n=12, p=0.35)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Successes'); plt.ylabel('Probability'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cf473368",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 6. Bernoulli — (p)\n",
    "\n",
    "Models one binary event: success or failure. It underlies binary labels and Bernoulli likelihoods in classification."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0245edaf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "p, outcome = 0.35, 1\n",
    "probability = p if outcome == 1 else 1-p\n",
    "print(f\"P(outcome={outcome}) = {probability:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f1a39c86",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7c382982",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.bernoulli(p=0.35)\n",
    "x = np.array([0, 1])\n",
    "plt.bar(x, d.pmf(x)); plt.xticks(x, ['Failure (0)', 'Success (1)'])\n",
    "plt.title('Bernoulli (p=0.35)'); plt.ylabel('Probability'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9a9cecae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Continuous distributions\n",
    "\n",
    "These distributions describe continuous-valued quantities. The curves below are probability density functions; probability corresponds to area over an interval."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3e8e7ad6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 7. Lognormal — (μ, σ²)\n",
    "\n",
    "Positive values whose logarithms follow a Normal distribution. Common for skewed quantities such as transaction sizes or durations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "48222a6d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "mu, sigma, x = 0, 0.5, 1.5\n",
    "pdf = math.exp(-(math.log(x)-mu)**2/(2*sigma**2))/(x*sigma*math.sqrt(2*math.pi))\n",
    "print(f\"Lognormal density at {x} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c7a27939",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "425d096a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.lognorm(s=0.5, scale=np.exp(0))\n",
    "x = np.linspace(0.01, 5, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, d.pdf(x)); plt.title('Lognormal (μ=0, σ=0.5)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('x'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3bbf3f31",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 8. Normal (Gaussian) — (μ, σ²)\n",
    "\n",
    "A symmetric bell-shaped distribution. It appears in noise models, statistical assumptions, and parameter initialization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2648f027",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "mu, sigma, x = 1, 1.5, 2\n",
    "pdf = math.exp(-0.5*((x-mu)/sigma)**2)/(sigma*math.sqrt(2*math.pi))\n",
    "print(f\"Normal density at {x} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dbf184d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "627247bc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.norm(loc=1, scale=1.5)\n",
    "x = np.linspace(-5, 7, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, d.pdf(x)); plt.title('Normal (μ=1, σ=1.5)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('x'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4b2582f6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 9. Standard Normal — (0, 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "The Normal distribution with mean 0 and standard deviation 1. Z-scores and normalized values often use this reference distribution."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f6d73141",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "z = 1.0\n",
    "pdf = math.exp(-z*z/2)/math.sqrt(2*math.pi)\n",
    "print(f\"Standard Normal density at z={z} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d33a1eaf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "33c4488a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.norm(loc=0, scale=1)\n",
    "z = np.linspace(-4, 4, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(z, d.pdf(z)); plt.title('Standard Normal N(0, 1)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('z-score'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e34e6388",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 10. Beta — (α, β)\n",
    "\n",
    "A distribution over values from 0 to 1. Useful for modeling probabilities, rates, and uncertainty about Bernoulli success probabilities."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2b86b268",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "alpha, beta, x = 2, 5, 0.3\n",
    "normalizer = math.gamma(alpha+beta)/(math.gamma(alpha)*math.gamma(beta))\n",
    "pdf = normalizer*x**(alpha-1)*(1-x)**(beta-1)\n",
    "print(f\"Beta density at {x} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9ef776b7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3be48596",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.beta(a=2, b=5)\n",
    "x = np.linspace(0, 1, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, d.pdf(x)); plt.title('Beta (α=2, β=5)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Probability'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7433f7a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 11. Gamma — (r, λ)\n",
    "\n",
    "A positive-valued distribution used for waiting times and rates. It is also a flexible prior in probabilistic models."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3fe5261c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "shape, scale, x = 2, 2, 3\n",
    "pdf = x**(shape-1)*math.exp(-x/scale)/(math.gamma(shape)*scale**shape)\n",
    "print(f\"Gamma density at {x} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1da6d0ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0824b60a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.gamma(a=2, scale=2)  # shape r=2; scale=2 (rate=0.5)\n",
    "x = np.linspace(0, 16, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, d.pdf(x)); plt.title('Gamma (shape=2, scale=2)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('x'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2738c0da",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 12. Uniform — (0, 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "Every value in the interval has equal density. Uniform sampling is used in simulation and parameter initialization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ccf3edb0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "a, b, x = 0, 1, 0.4\n",
    "pdf = 1/(b-a) if a <= x <= b else 0\n",
    "print(f\"Uniform density at {x} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9d485305",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c78ee9d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.uniform(loc=0, scale=1)\n",
    "x = np.linspace(-0.2, 1.2, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, d.pdf(x)); plt.title('Uniform (0, 1)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('x'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f0ab9d5b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 13. Cauchy (Standard) — (0, 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "A heavy-tailed distribution with undefined mean and variance. It is useful as a robust statistical example and caution against relying on averages."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d856743c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "location, scale, x = 0, 1, 1\n",
    "pdf = 1/(math.pi*scale*(1+((x-location)/scale)**2))\n",
    "print(f\"Cauchy density at {x} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "32880931",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "df065f5f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.cauchy(loc=0, scale=1)\n",
    "x = np.linspace(-8, 8, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, d.pdf(x)); plt.title('Standard Cauchy (0, 1)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('x'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d02f8986",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 14. Chi-Squared — (ν)\n",
    "\n",
    "The sum of squared standard Normal variables. It is used in statistical tests and variance-related inference."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3504dcbe",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "nu, x = 4, 3\n",
    "pdf = x**(nu/2-1)*math.exp(-x/2)/(2**(nu/2)*math.gamma(nu/2))\n",
    "print(f\"Chi-squared density at {x} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "10d4970b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3103e8d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.chi2(df=4)\n",
    "x = np.linspace(0, 18, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, d.pdf(x)); plt.title('Chi-Squared (ν=4)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('x'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "77f651a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 15. Exponential — (λ)\n",
    "\n",
    "Models waiting time between events in a Poisson process. Useful for event-time and reliability modeling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b40a269e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "rate, x = 0.5, 2\n",
    "pdf = rate*math.exp(-rate*x) if x >= 0 else 0\n",
    "print(f\"Exponential density at {x} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5a2736f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f9e5690b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.expon(scale=2)  # rate λ=0.5\n",
    "x = np.linspace(0, 12, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, d.pdf(x)); plt.title('Exponential (λ=0.5)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Waiting time'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8e9cc4ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 16. Weibull — (k, λ)\n",
    "\n",
    "A flexible lifetime and reliability distribution. Its shape parameter allows increasing, decreasing, or constant hazard rates."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9eaea065",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pure Python — evaluate one value\n",
    "import math\n",
    "shape, scale, x = 1.5, 2, 3\n",
    "pdf = (shape/scale)*(x/scale)**(shape-1)*math.exp(-(x/scale)**shape)\n",
    "print(f\"Weibull density at {x} = {pdf:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2ff4c3b2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**SciPy + Matplotlib — visualize the same distribution.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7b684735",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = stats.weibull_min(c=1.5, scale=2)\n",
    "x = np.linspace(0, 8, 400)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, d.pdf(x)); plt.title('Weibull (k=1.5, scale=2)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Lifetime'); plt.ylabel('Density'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
