   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x = np.linspace(-4, 4, 200)\n",
    "plt.plot(x, relu(x)); plt.title('ReLU'); plt.grid(alpha=.2); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ab6df7be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Sigmoid\n",
    "\n",
    "Maps values to (0, 1). Often used to produce a binary-classification probability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "791b262d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import math\n",
    "\n",
    "def sigmoid(x):\n",
    "    return 1/(1+math.exp(-x))\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Sigmoid(1) =', round(sigmoid(1), 5))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
